<p>Your dad wears glasses every single day. He puts them on before his first cup of coffee and takes them off before bed. They affect how clearly he sees his phone, his computer, the road, and your beautiful face. And there is a good chance the pair he is wearing right now is two or three years old, scratched up, and no longer exactly right for his prescription.</p>

<p>A new pair of glasses is one of the most practical and most personal Father&#8217;s Day gifts you can give. Picked well, with the right lenses and frames chosen for how he lives, it is something he will use every day for years. This guide covers what to look for, what actually matters in eyewear, and how to get it right, even if you have never bought glasses as a gift before.</p>

